quran[9]{c,v,t}:
  21,36,"And whenever the disbelievers see you, they only take you for mockery, (saying:) ‘Is this the one who speaks (ill) of your gods?’ But it is they who deny the remembrance of the Most-Compassionate (Lord)."
  21,37,Human being was created hasty (and impatient by his disposition). I shall soon show you My signs. So do not ask Me to hasten (the punishment).
  21,38,And they say: ‘When will this promise (of punishment) be fulfilled if you are truthful?’
  21,39,"If only the disbelievers knew that a time would come when they would not be able to stop the Fire from (burning) their faces and their backs, nor would they be helped (then they would not seek to hasten it)."
  21,40,"Instead, it will come upon them suddenly and confound them. So, neither will they be able to avert it nor be granted respite."
  21,41,And certainly messengers were mocked before you. But those who ridiculed them were overtaken by what they used to mock.
  21,42,"Say: ‘Who can guard you by night and day from (the punishment of) the Most-Compassionate (Lord)?’ Instead, they are disregardful of their Lord’s remembrance."
  21,43,Do they have gods besides Us who can defend them (from the punishment)? They can neither help themselves nor will they be given protection against Us.
  21,44,"Instead, We provided enjoyment to these (Meccans) and their fathers until they lived on for a long time. Do they not see how We are shrinking the land (under their control) from its borders? So, are they the ones who will prevail?"
